    <!-- ═══ 09 · IN CAPE TOWN OR ONLINE ═══ -->
    <section id="in-cape-town" class="bg-background">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28 max-w-4xl ctc-reveal">
        <h2 class="font-heading ctc-gold-text text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[44px] leading-tight mb-10">In Cape Town or online</h2>

        <div class="font-body text-lg text-foreground/78 leading-relaxed space-y-7 max-w-[65ch]">
          <p>For people based in Cape Town, I see clients in person at a private consulting room in Newlands, in the Southern Suburbs. The room is quiet and comfortable, with natural light and a garden outlook, and it sits apart from the demands of home and work. Some people find that a defined place, at a defined time, makes it easier to give the conversation their full attention. Appointments are arranged in advance, and the address and arrival details are shared privately once an appointment is confirmed.</p>

          <p>Sessions are also available online by video call, for people elsewhere in South Africa and further afield, and for anyone who simply finds remote work more practical. Online counselling can be easier to sustain around work, travel, family life or distance, and some people settle into the conversation more quickly when they are speaking from their own environment.</p>

          <p>The substance of the work does not change with the format. What matters is whether the relationship is useful, and whether the process is moving you towards what you came for.</p>
        </div>

        <p class="font-heading ctc-gold-text text-2xl md:text-[28px] italic leading-snug mt-12 mb-14">The work is the same. The room changes.</p>

